		{
			"name": "Warehouse (gRPC)",
			"description": "Requirement 2 - stock lives in a standalone Go gRPC service (services/warehouse) with its own PostgreSQL database.\n\nSuggested run order:\n1. Login (Customer) / Login (Admin)\n2. Get Stock via Product Details\n3. Reserve Stock (Create Order)\n4. Stock After Reserve\n5. Release Stock (Cancel Order, Admin)\n6. Stock After Cancel\n7. Insufficient Stock -> 409\n8. Warehouse Down -> 503 (set {{run_warehouse_down}} = true after `docker compose stop warehouse`)\n9. Race Condition (Proof): run scripts/proof/race-condition.ps1, then set {{run_race}} = true and send item 5.\n\nSeeded warehouse stock: product 1 = 1 unit (race target), products 2..8 = 100 units each.\n\nItems 4 and 5 are skipped by default so the whole collection can run green without stopping containers; flip the variables to run the two manual proofs.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Login (Customer)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
									"var body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('customer token stored in {{token}}', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(body.data && body.data.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
									"});",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.data.token);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Accept",
